WEBVTT


00:01:00.516 --> 00:01:02.250
We got vultures circling here.


00:01:02.251 --> 00:01:05.386
Lacs to the neck, chest, hands,
shoulder-- take your pick.


00:01:05.387 --> 00:01:07.104
How many times
was she stabbed?


00:01:07.105 --> 00:01:08.640
She's lost
too much blood.


00:01:08.641 --> 00:01:10.441
Jed! Need a large bore IV, stat!


00:01:10.442 --> 00:01:12.143
Neighbours watched it happen,
and no one even called the cops.


00:01:12.144 --> 00:01:14.011
We did what we could, but--


00:01:14.012 --> 00:01:15.111
Does she have a name?


00:01:15.112 --> 00:01:16.279
Allison Parks.


00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:17.648
Okay, Allison, stay with us.


00:01:24.587 --> 00:01:26.322
Gonna have to jump her.
Gimme 360.


00:01:26.323 --> 00:01:28.258
Charge 360.


00:01:33.047 --> 00:01:34.847
Oh, my god.


00:01:40.069 --> 00:01:41.587
He loved me.


00:01:41.588 --> 00:01:43.772
Wait a minute.
She's trying to say something.


00:01:43.773 --> 00:01:46.458
Clear!


00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.544
Kaitlyn! Kaitlyn!


00:01:54.383 --> 00:01:56.317
You all right?


00:01:59.688 --> 00:02:00.922
He loved me.


00:02:04.026 --> 00:02:05.825
Where is she?!


00:02:05.826 --> 00:02:08.429
Oh, thank God.
What
happened?


00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:11.932
Shit, Kate, your heart just
stopped... that's all.


00:02:11.933 --> 00:02:15.119
Hey, hey, hey!
Take it easy.


00:02:18.123 --> 00:02:21.057
You've taken
some punishment today.


00:02:24.362 --> 00:02:27.129
What the hell happened in there?


00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:28.464
What do you mean?


00:02:28.465 --> 00:02:31.501
Well, grabbing a patient in the
middle of an ICD?


00:02:31.502 --> 00:02:32.502
You have a death wish?


00:02:32.503 --> 00:02:35.354
No, she was lucid.
She was awake.


00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:37.022
Who?


00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:40.560
The girl. That girl.
Did she make it?


00:02:40.561 --> 00:02:42.795
Let's just worry
about you, okay?


00:02:42.796 --> 00:02:44.313
She was responsive.


00:02:44.314 --> 00:02:46.381
She was scared to death,
but she was responsive.


00:02:46.382 --> 00:02:48.032
What are you talking about,
sweetie?


00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:50.268
She looked right at me.


00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.869
She spoke to me. She was trying
to talk to me.


00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:55.940
She was trying to...
tell me something.


00:02:55.941 --> 00:02:57.642
That girl had been stabbed over
a dozen times.


00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.744
You have any idea
how much blood she lost?


00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:01.446
She couldn't have said a word.


00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:04.148
No... No, she--
she spoke to me.


00:03:04.149 --> 00:03:06.167
She was trying to tell me--


00:03:06.168 --> 00:03:10.004
I think she was trying to tell
me who stabbed her.


00:03:10.005 --> 00:03:13.105
Honey, that girl was dead


00:03:13.106 --> 00:03:15.242
before she ever came
through those doors.


00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:47.907
So, let me guess...
no witnesses, right?


00:03:47.908 --> 00:03:50.192
14 witnesses
watched her go down.


00:03:50.193 --> 00:03:54.261
Watched it? What do you mean,
"Watched it?"


00:03:54.262 --> 00:03:55.697
Did you get statements?


00:03:55.698 --> 00:03:57.215
Heard a scuffle, they looked out
the window,


00:03:57.216 --> 00:03:58.966
and they watched a little girl
get stabbed


00:03:58.967 --> 00:04:00.535
like they was watching
television.


00:04:00.536 --> 00:04:02.121
Here's the best part:
no one bothered to call 911.


00:04:05.257 --> 00:04:06.724
Well, that is just wonderful.


00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.318
Do me a favour, will you?


00:04:17.319 --> 00:04:18.618
Grab some shots
from the windows,


00:04:18.619 --> 00:04:20.120
looking down on this area.


00:04:20.121 --> 00:04:22.088
Sure thing.


00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:34.966
So why would no one call the
cops, huh? Tell me that.


00:04:34.967 --> 00:04:38.271
Listen, man, I find that fact a
bit depressing,


00:04:38.272 --> 00:04:41.774
but... not us.


00:04:41.775 --> 00:04:45.076
14 people means 14 witnesses.
Somebody saw something.


00:04:45.077 --> 00:04:47.196
Best I could get was
a vague description.


00:04:47.197 --> 00:04:50.949
Male. Race unknown.
Black jacket.


00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.683
Maybe a blue baseball cap.


00:04:52.684 --> 00:04:56.487
And not one person caught a
glimpse of the perp's face?


00:04:56.488 --> 00:05:00.792
It's too dark out here.


00:05:00.793 --> 00:05:02.994
How long's this lamp been out?


00:05:02.995 --> 00:05:05.862
I don't know.
It's a good question.


00:05:08.417 --> 00:05:10.517
Well, do me a favour,
will you?


00:05:10.518 --> 00:05:13.720
Go ask somebody.
Thanks.


00:05:13.721 --> 00:05:15.655
Started off to be
such a great day.


00:05:39.329 --> 00:05:41.796
Kate! Whoa. Kaitlyn.


00:05:41.797 --> 00:05:42.832
What?


00:05:42.833 --> 00:05:44.233
Where do you think you're going?


00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:46.002
You're still in shock from the
defib. You need to rest.


00:05:46.003 --> 00:05:47.401
No, I gotta go home.


00:05:47.402 --> 00:05:49.671
Hey! You can go home
when you've been released.


00:05:49.672 --> 00:05:52.305
How many times have you had the
same conversation


00:05:52.306 --> 00:05:53.675
with your own patients?


00:05:53.676 --> 00:05:55.276
I-- No, I have to go home and
take care of my mom.


00:05:55.277 --> 00:05:57.177
She can't be without me
for this long.


00:05:57.178 --> 00:05:58.646
I'll check in on her.
Just tell me where I need to--


00:05:58.647 --> 00:06:00.382
Val, I'm going. I'm sorry,
but my mother needs me.


00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.752
How's she holding up?


00:06:04.753 --> 00:06:07.154
Well, uh, they gave her
six weeks,


00:06:07.155 --> 00:06:10.857
and six months later, she's
still here, so... there's that.


00:06:10.858 --> 00:06:13.994
Look, take the next
couple days off, okay?


00:06:13.995 --> 00:06:15.830
I'll cover for you.


00:06:15.831 --> 00:06:17.798
Go be with your mom
and rest.


00:06:17.799 --> 00:06:19.600
I mean really rest.


00:06:19.601 --> 00:06:21.869
And call me if you need
anything. Anything.


00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:24.304
Thank you.


00:06:24.305 --> 00:06:26.723
Oh, and say hi
to your mom for me..


00:06:26.724 --> 00:06:27.607
Okay.


00:06:45.242 --> 00:06:47.759
Ma'am? Ma'am! Are you okay?


00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.800
We got vultures circling here.


00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:59.636
Lacs to the chest, hands, neck,
shoulder-- take your pick.


00:06:59.637 --> 00:07:02.006
How many times
was she stabbed?


00:07:02.007 --> 00:07:04.575
She's lost
too much blood.


00:07:04.576 --> 00:07:08.262
Jed! Need a large bore IV, stat!


00:07:08.263 --> 00:07:09.630
Bunch of neighbours
watched it happen.


00:07:09.631 --> 00:07:11.232
No one even called the cops.


00:07:11.233 --> 00:07:13.467
We did what we could, but--


00:07:14.868 --> 00:07:17.604
Gonna have to jump her.
Gimme 360.


00:07:17.605 --> 00:07:19.539
Charge 360.


00:07:28.483 --> 00:07:30.917
He loved me.


00:07:30.918 --> 00:07:32.102
Clear!


00:08:24.352 --> 00:08:25.452
What's wrong?


00:08:25.453 --> 00:08:27.754
Nothing.


00:08:27.755 --> 00:08:29.823
You look tired.


00:08:29.824 --> 00:08:30.991
You're one to talk.


00:08:30.992 --> 00:08:35.494
Don't be stubborn.
Tell me.


00:08:35.495 --> 00:08:37.747
It was a nightmare.
That's all.


00:08:37.748 --> 00:08:39.665
Everything's fine.


00:08:39.666 --> 00:08:43.151
You know, you don't have to
sleep in that chair every night.


00:08:43.152 --> 00:08:45.454
It's fine.
It's not!


00:08:45.455 --> 00:08:48.490
The chair is no good.


00:08:48.491 --> 00:08:50.158
That is why you're tired.


00:08:50.159 --> 00:08:53.661
Now, you have your own bed.
You should use it.


00:08:53.662 --> 00:08:55.163
Swallow.


00:09:01.087 --> 00:09:02.620
You know, I just
worry about you.


00:09:02.621 --> 00:09:04.122
Don't.


00:09:04.123 --> 00:09:06.040
Something is troubling you.


00:09:06.041 --> 00:09:08.508
Now, I may be sick,
but I'm not stupid.


00:09:12.797 --> 00:09:15.750
It's a patient.
Died yesterday.


00:09:15.751 --> 00:09:19.236
She was stabbed to death.


00:09:19.237 --> 00:09:21.355
It was bad.


00:09:21.356 --> 00:09:23.856
I'm sure she suffered.


00:09:23.857 --> 00:09:25.992
I'm sure you did
everything you could.


00:09:25.993 --> 00:09:30.729
No, I didn't.


00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:33.533
I couldn't do anything.


00:09:33.534 --> 00:09:36.085
I looked right at this girl,
Mom. I looked right at her.


00:09:36.086 --> 00:09:39.170
And she-- she was
looking back at me,


00:09:39.171 --> 00:09:41.173
like, into me.


00:09:41.174 --> 00:09:45.078
Like she wanted something. Like
she wanted me to do something.


00:09:45.079 --> 00:09:47.062
Like she was trying to reach
out, and--


00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:55.053
Heavens.


00:09:59.741 --> 00:10:03.294
Honey, just let it go.


00:10:03.295 --> 00:10:07.949
It's all right.


00:10:09.918 --> 00:10:11.919
We're at the scene of a grisly
murder of a local woman


00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.921
where police have made
no arrests at this point,


00:10:13.922 --> 00:10:15.788
and they have few leads.


00:10:15.789 --> 00:10:18.058
The attack appears to be a
mugging gone wrong.


00:10:18.059 --> 00:10:20.793
The tragic tale of
a desperate criminal


00:10:20.794 --> 00:10:23.797
who falls upon
an unsuspecting victim


00:10:23.798 --> 00:10:26.749
in a dark and somewhat
isolated location.


00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:28.284
No, that's not right.


00:10:28.285 --> 00:10:30.635
Allison Parks was simply in the
wrong place at the wrong time,


00:10:30.636 --> 00:10:32.739
and unfortunately,
random crimes such as this


00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:34.257
are fairly difficult to solve.


00:10:39.229 --> 00:10:40.664
I can't stop thinking
about that girl.


00:10:40.665 --> 00:10:44.217
Yeah, I know. It was horrible.


00:10:44.218 --> 00:10:46.118
But the cops'll find the guy;
I'm sure.


00:10:46.119 --> 00:10:47.853
No, they're giving up.


00:10:47.854 --> 00:10:49.187
What are you talking about?


00:10:49.188 --> 00:10:51.156
They're not even looking in the
right place.


00:10:51.157 --> 00:10:52.625
And you know the right place?


00:10:52.626 --> 00:10:53.925
Well, whoever killed Allison
knew her.


00:10:53.926 --> 00:10:55.193
Whoa. Allison?


00:10:55.194 --> 00:10:57.596
She said, "He loved me."


00:10:57.597 --> 00:10:58.696
Okay, do you hear yourself?
You're not making any sense.


00:10:58.697 --> 00:11:00.182
She told me.


00:11:00.183 --> 00:11:03.033
That girl didn't tell you
anything. She was dead.


00:11:04.786 --> 00:11:06.487
Okay, so, what?
You think I'm hallucinating?


00:11:06.488 --> 00:11:08.022
You think I'm just
making all this up?


00:11:08.023 --> 00:11:11.609
No, I don't.


00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:13.911
Look, honey, I know you, okay?


00:11:13.912 --> 00:11:15.930
And you always want to believe
that you can help,


00:11:15.931 --> 00:11:19.950
but sometimes we do everything,
and it's just not enough.


00:11:19.951 --> 00:11:21.884
Yeah...


00:11:21.885 --> 00:11:24.354
We do what we do, okay?


00:11:24.355 --> 00:11:26.524
Let the cops do what they do.


00:12:19.239 --> 00:12:21.175
Allison?


00:12:23.211 --> 00:12:25.178
Allison, is that you?


00:12:28.248 --> 00:12:30.983
Oh, Jesus, Mary and Joseph.


00:12:33.488 --> 00:12:37.055
You look just like her.


00:12:37.056 --> 00:12:39.725
I thought I was seeing a ghost.


00:12:42.546 --> 00:12:44.278
So, what'd you find?


00:12:44.279 --> 00:12:47.950
Whole lot of nothing.


00:12:47.951 --> 00:12:50.334
Well, nice work then.


00:12:50.335 --> 00:12:52.637
Gave witnesses a bunch of
baseball hats to look at.


00:12:52.638 --> 00:12:53.638
It's pointless.


00:12:53.639 --> 00:12:55.640
What about the knife wound?


00:12:55.641 --> 00:12:59.310
Nothing conclusive, but the lab
said the wounds, and I quote,


00:12:59.311 --> 00:13:01.612
"Were consistent with a large
kitchen knife,


00:13:01.613 --> 00:13:04.283
possessing precise serration,
approximately six inches long.


00:13:04.284 --> 00:13:07.285
Yeah? Yeah, that'd do it.


00:13:07.286 --> 00:13:09.054
I like the part about precise
serration. Precise serration.


00:13:09.055 --> 00:13:12.489
It's like the lab guy is going
shopping for a wedding gift.


00:13:12.491 --> 00:13:14.424
So, what? Some tweaker?


00:13:14.425 --> 00:13:16.092
He tries to sneak a couple of
bucks out of this girl?


00:13:16.093 --> 00:13:17.661
Is that what happens?


00:13:17.662 --> 00:13:19.263
Then she starts screaming
and he just flips out?


00:13:19.264 --> 00:13:21.348
He's got a big ol' knife
and he uses it to shut her up.


00:13:25.569 --> 00:13:28.038
I don't get a lot of visitors.


00:13:28.039 --> 00:13:29.956
Thank you.


00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:36.128
Still can't believe she's gone.


00:13:36.129 --> 00:13:40.332
Tragedy.


00:13:40.333 --> 00:13:43.235
How did you two meet?


00:13:43.236 --> 00:13:46.004
School.


00:13:46.005 --> 00:13:49.424
Oh. Classmates.


00:13:49.425 --> 00:13:51.743
I heard there were witnesses.
Did you see anything?


00:13:51.744 --> 00:13:54.948
I, uh-- No.


00:13:56.915 --> 00:13:59.918
Are you-- are you hungry?


00:13:59.919 --> 00:14:03.155
I could heat up
some frozen dinners.


00:14:03.156 --> 00:14:07.675
But your window is-- it looks
right out onto the courtyard.


00:14:07.676 --> 00:14:09.378
You didn't see anything?


00:14:09.379 --> 00:14:12.212
Uh, uh...


00:14:12.213 --> 00:14:16.784
I was out, like I told you.


00:14:16.785 --> 00:14:20.488
But I heard all about it from
the couple in 3E.


00:14:22.289 --> 00:14:24.208
Horrible.


00:14:24.209 --> 00:14:25.626
I just-- Poor Alli.


00:14:25.627 --> 00:14:28.061
Just screamed and screamed
and screamed.


00:14:31.499 --> 00:14:33.399
Nobody should have to hear that.


00:14:36.153 --> 00:14:38.788
I don't understand.


00:14:38.789 --> 00:14:40.590
Why didn't anyone
call the police?


00:14:40.591 --> 00:14:43.559
It was so awful.


00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:46.578
So loud.


00:14:46.579 --> 00:14:51.401
Everybody figured someone else,
surely, would call the cops,


00:14:51.402 --> 00:14:54.869
you know, after
all that screaming.


00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:58.522
That's what happened--
must've been what happened.


00:14:58.523 --> 00:15:02.628
Everybody just thought
the same thing:


00:15:02.629 --> 00:15:05.946
that somebody else was
gonna take care of it.


00:15:05.947 --> 00:15:10.785
It's not that hard to
understand, really.


00:15:10.786 --> 00:15:12.922
I thought you said
you weren't here.


00:15:14.923 --> 00:15:16.057
I wasn't.


00:15:18.559 --> 00:15:20.927
So what if more than one person
called the police.


00:15:20.928 --> 00:15:25.015
Every single one of you should
have been calling the police.


00:15:25.016 --> 00:15:26.751
What do you want from me?


00:15:29.135 --> 00:15:30.604
Sorry. I'm sorry.


00:15:30.605 --> 00:15:33.307
It's just--


00:15:33.307 --> 00:15:35.308
The police, they think
it was random,


00:15:35.309 --> 00:15:37.176
that it was a mugging.


00:15:37.177 --> 00:15:39.012
Yeah.


00:15:39.013 --> 00:15:40.981
Yeah, some crackhead.


00:15:43.151 --> 00:15:45.084
Do you believe that?


00:15:47.087 --> 00:15:49.587
If that's what they say.
What do I know?


00:15:49.588 --> 00:15:51.940
I'm just trying
to make sense of all this.


00:15:51.941 --> 00:15:54.376
I don't understand who would
want to hurt Allison.


00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:00.982
She said something
to me about, um...


00:16:00.983 --> 00:16:03.518
about a man in her life.
Someone she cared about.


00:16:03.519 --> 00:16:04.903
Does that ring any bells?


00:16:04.904 --> 00:16:08.339
Listen, I've explained
all this to the detective.


00:16:09.976 --> 00:16:14.362
I barely knew her,
all right?


00:16:14.363 --> 00:16:16.363
She was my neighbour.


00:16:16.364 --> 00:16:19.283
Seemed like a sweet girl.


00:16:22.386 --> 00:16:25.923
I wave at her, in the hallway.


00:16:25.923 --> 00:16:27.925
She gave me the keys
to her apartment


00:16:27.926 --> 00:16:29.576
so I could go in
and water her plants


00:16:29.577 --> 00:16:33.696
when she would go away
with her boyfriend.


00:16:33.697 --> 00:16:36.399
That's it.


00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:38.335
Her boyfriend.


00:16:38.335 --> 00:16:41.637
Yeah, scruffy kid.
Artsy type.


00:16:41.638 --> 00:16:43.106
But he may have
been around for months.


00:16:43.107 --> 00:16:44.107
What's his name?


00:16:44.108 --> 00:16:46.425
You and Allison were close,


00:16:46.426 --> 00:16:49.228
and you never talked
about her boyfriend?


00:16:51.764 --> 00:16:54.399
I've bothered you enough. Thank
you so much for the coffee.


00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:55.868
I'm gonna-- I should go.


00:16:55.869 --> 00:16:59.804
Oh, oh, wait, wait, wait.


00:16:59.805 --> 00:17:03.108
We're just getting
to know each other.


00:17:03.109 --> 00:17:05.043
I can't send you
back out in the cold.


00:17:05.045 --> 00:17:07.294
No, really, I should take off.


00:17:07.295 --> 00:17:09.330
Let me make us some dinner.


00:17:11.267 --> 00:17:13.735
I have some frozen dinners
I can warm up.


00:17:13.736 --> 00:17:15.236
You like brandy?


00:17:15.237 --> 00:17:18.973
No, but you know, I wouldn't
say no to a glass of water.


00:17:18.974 --> 00:17:20.925
Oh, that's no trouble at all.


00:17:25.897 --> 00:17:28.983
Like ice?


00:17:28.984 --> 00:17:31.185
You want ice, sweetheart?


00:18:49.493 --> 00:18:51.426
Ow.


00:20:16.459 --> 00:20:17.758
Hey, you all right?


00:20:19.327 --> 00:20:21.428
Where is he?


00:20:21.429 --> 00:20:22.796
Who? Where is who?


00:20:22.797 --> 00:20:24.965
The guy with the knife!
Where is he?


00:20:24.966 --> 00:20:26.249
Who?


00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:28.885
The guy, where'd he go?


00:20:28.886 --> 00:20:29.852
There's nobody here.


00:20:38.896 --> 00:20:41.498
Okay, how about
we try this again?


00:20:41.499 --> 00:20:44.333
I am Detective Peter Rafferty,
and you are not


00:20:44.334 --> 00:20:48.137
a friend or relative of
Allison Parks, correct?


00:20:48.138 --> 00:20:49.370
Correct.


00:20:49.371 --> 00:20:50.990
Did you know Miss Parks?


00:20:50.991 --> 00:20:52.391
No.


00:20:52.392 --> 00:20:53.859
But you have a perfectly
good reason


00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:56.412
for snooping around
her apartment.


00:20:56.413 --> 00:20:58.614
I was one of the nurses on duty
when she came in.


00:20:58.615 --> 00:21:01.600
I was there when she died.


00:21:01.601 --> 00:21:03.067
I'm gonna call that a "no."


00:21:03.068 --> 00:21:06.704
I didn't take anything.
I was just looking around.


00:21:06.705 --> 00:21:08.257
Looking for what?


00:21:08.258 --> 00:21:09.423
Anything.


00:21:09.424 --> 00:21:11.942
Somebody has to
find out who did this.


00:21:11.943 --> 00:21:14.278
You're right.
Someone needs to find out.


00:21:14.279 --> 00:21:16.080
I happen to be the
lead investigator.


00:21:16.081 --> 00:21:21.084
I saw you on the news. Didn't
exactly inspire any confidence.


00:21:21.085 --> 00:21:24.021
Ma'am, crimes like this are
fairly complicated,


00:21:24.022 --> 00:21:26.640
but the system works.


00:21:26.641 --> 00:21:30.110
Given enough time,
the bad guy always gets caught.


00:21:30.111 --> 00:21:32.963
You believe any of that?


00:21:32.964 --> 00:21:34.464
I'll call that a "no."


00:21:34.465 --> 00:21:37.600
Whoever did this,
Allison knew her. She told me.


00:21:37.601 --> 00:21:39.236
Miss Parks told you?


00:21:39.237 --> 00:21:41.854
She looked at me.


00:21:41.855 --> 00:21:43.956
She looked right
at me and she said,


00:21:43.957 --> 00:21:47.477
"He loved me."


00:21:47.478 --> 00:21:48.777
It was the last thing she said.


00:21:48.778 --> 00:21:50.112
Yeah, I know,
I'm just some nurse,


00:21:50.113 --> 00:21:52.381
but I don't think that's
something I would say


00:21:52.382 --> 00:21:54.316
if my attacker was
some random crack addict.


00:21:55.934 --> 00:21:57.970
Ma'am, the hospital said that
she died in the ambulance.


00:21:57.971 --> 00:22:00.822
That's not-- no, that's wrong.


00:22:00.823 --> 00:22:02.924
Well, actually, right here.


00:22:02.925 --> 00:22:05.776
"Despite all efforts, I was
unable to kick-start her heart."


00:22:05.777 --> 00:22:07.313
That's what it says.


00:22:07.314 --> 00:22:09.781
Well, sometimes there are
discrepancies.


00:22:09.782 --> 00:22:11.065
Between alive and dead?


00:22:11.066 --> 00:22:12.316
She was alive.


00:22:12.317 --> 00:22:14.435
That's fine, ma'am.
Go on, please.


00:22:14.436 --> 00:22:16.820
This wasn't a mugging.


00:22:16.821 --> 00:22:20.191
Whoever killed Allison knew her,
loved her.


00:22:20.192 --> 00:22:21.524
If you have any evidence


00:22:21.525 --> 00:22:22.894
suggesting that there's some
sort of conspiracy--


00:22:22.895 --> 00:22:25.930
Even if the hospital was wrong,
which is highly possible,


00:22:25.931 --> 00:22:28.198
considering how badly they
screwed up on my tonsils--


00:22:28.199 --> 00:22:31.634
even if-- I mean, "He loved me"
could mean anything.


00:22:31.635 --> 00:22:33.353
It could mean a puppy she had
when she was nine years old.


00:22:33.354 --> 00:22:35.722
No, look, that's not it.
I know what she meant.


00:22:37.273 --> 00:22:40.577
So you went to her apartment?


00:22:40.578 --> 00:22:42.777
Yeah, I felt like I had to
help her. Somebody has to.


00:22:42.778 --> 00:22:46.533
Why were you running?


00:22:46.534 --> 00:22:50.302
I-- I thought I saw someone.


00:22:52.038 --> 00:22:54.773
You thought you saw
someone in the apartment?


00:22:54.774 --> 00:22:56.492
No...


00:22:56.493 --> 00:22:57.960
Well, I--


00:22:57.961 --> 00:23:00.362
Look, it was dark, you know...


00:23:00.363 --> 00:23:04.917
and... I probably
just got spooked.


00:23:04.918 --> 00:23:08.586
And... this is gonna sound
really crazy, but...


00:23:10.272 --> 00:23:13.907
It was like I was imagining
the murder through her eyes.


00:23:16.178 --> 00:23:19.497
I was there.


00:23:19.498 --> 00:23:21.799
And then, you showed up,
and it was gone.


00:23:24.269 --> 00:23:26.638
Just out of curiosity,


00:23:26.639 --> 00:23:28.422
are you currently using
any psychiatric drugs?


00:23:28.423 --> 00:23:30.724
Go to hell.


00:23:30.725 --> 00:23:35.112
"Just out of curiosity."
That's real subtle.


00:23:35.113 --> 00:23:37.047
It's not like you weren't
thinking it too.


00:23:38.882 --> 00:23:42.118
Miss Monahan. Kate.
Hold up, please.


00:23:42.119 --> 00:23:44.720
Are you arresting me? Because
if not, I'm gonna go home.


00:23:44.721 --> 00:23:47.656
Look, I am sorry about
Detective Canto back there.


00:23:47.657 --> 00:23:50.475
He's a good cop, just not always
known for his tact.


00:23:50.476 --> 00:23:51.677
Well, whatever. Forget it.


00:23:53.862 --> 00:23:55.196
Take this, please.


00:23:55.197 --> 00:23:57.816
If you remember anything,
anything at all,


00:23:57.817 --> 00:24:00.785
or if you just wanna talk,
feel free to call me anytime.


00:24:06.492 --> 00:24:08.327
You know, I'm not
the bad guy here.


00:24:18.237 --> 00:24:19.970
I don't know;
it's hard to explain.


00:24:19.971 --> 00:24:22.372
It felt like I was really there.


00:24:22.373 --> 00:24:25.341
But it was just like your
imagination, right?


00:24:27.345 --> 00:24:29.279
I don't know.


00:24:29.280 --> 00:24:31.181
I mean, it felt so real.


00:24:31.182 --> 00:24:33.016
Do you hear yourself?


00:24:33.017 --> 00:24:34.651
Yeah, I do.


00:24:34.652 --> 00:24:37.620
Your brain was hit
with enough voltage...


00:24:37.621 --> 00:24:39.506
I'm just glad you're not talking
to trees at this point.


00:24:39.506 --> 00:24:40.806
Thank you. Thanks.


00:24:40.807 --> 00:24:42.908
Hey, I don't understand
what you were doing


00:24:42.909 --> 00:24:44.644
in the girl's apartment
in the first place.


00:24:49.199 --> 00:24:52.267
This... is Allison's boyfriend,


00:24:52.268 --> 00:24:55.754
and I think I know
where I can find him.


00:24:55.755 --> 00:24:57.489
You took this from a crime
scene?


00:24:57.490 --> 00:25:01.060
The cops aren't doing anything.
Nobody's doing anything but me.


00:25:01.061 --> 00:25:05.881
Maybe I could help you schedule
some time up on the 4th floor.


00:25:05.882 --> 00:25:07.082
Oh, my god.


00:25:07.083 --> 00:25:08.566
I didn't mean it like that.


00:25:08.567 --> 00:25:11.418
Listen, Valerie, I don't need
a stupid shrink.


00:25:11.419 --> 00:25:14.121
I need somebody I can trust.
I need somebody who believes me.


00:25:14.122 --> 00:25:15.574
You're my best friend.


00:25:15.575 --> 00:25:18.509
Kaitlyn, you need to drop this
before you get yourself killed.


00:25:33.507 --> 00:25:34.707
Katie?


00:25:34.708 --> 00:25:36.410
Sorry, I'm running late, Mom.


00:25:36.411 --> 00:25:39.179
It'll be ready in about ten.


00:26:01.701 --> 00:26:03.367
Mom, are you okay?


00:26:04.837 --> 00:26:06.422
Mom!


00:26:08.106 --> 00:26:10.208
Mom? Oh, God. Mom!


00:26:11.978 --> 00:26:14.445
Listen to me. Listen to me, Mom.
You're having--


00:26:14.446 --> 00:26:16.280
Listen to me! You're having an
allergic reaction.


00:26:16.281 --> 00:26:18.281
Just stay focused. Please stay
focused on me, right now.


00:26:18.282 --> 00:26:19.616
I need you to calm down.


00:26:19.617 --> 00:26:24.037
Breathe. This is epinephrine.
Watch.


00:26:24.038 --> 00:26:27.107
It's adrenaline for the
swelling.


00:26:27.108 --> 00:26:29.810
You're gonna feel a little
pinch, and you're gonna be fine.


00:26:29.811 --> 00:26:32.229
All right, try and slow down
your breath.


00:26:32.230 --> 00:26:34.129
Slow down your breath.
Mom? Look at me. Look at me.


00:26:34.131 --> 00:26:36.599
Breathe. Breathe.


00:26:37.601 --> 00:26:39.201
There you go.


00:26:39.202 --> 00:26:41.136
Good.


00:26:51.832 --> 00:26:53.934
It's okay.


00:26:53.935 --> 00:26:56.168
You gotta stop scaring me
like that.


00:26:59.273 --> 00:27:00.705
What would I do without you?


00:27:49.669 --> 00:27:52.471
Allison was taken from us
suddenly,


00:27:52.472 --> 00:27:56.291
and without warning.


00:27:56.292 --> 00:27:59.794
Her death was random
and heartbreaking.


00:28:02.231 --> 00:28:06.818
It should remind us all


00:28:06.819 --> 00:28:11.688
to cherish the short time we
have upon this earth.


00:28:15.227 --> 00:28:19.414
Today may be filled
with sadness,


00:28:19.415 --> 00:28:24.084
yet we take comfort
in our knowledge


00:28:24.085 --> 00:28:29.039
that while Allison's body


00:28:29.040 --> 00:28:32.225
has passed on,


00:28:32.226 --> 00:28:34.762
her soul remains with us,


00:28:34.763 --> 00:28:38.597
now and forever.


00:28:38.598 --> 00:28:42.301
Her memory...


00:28:42.303 --> 00:28:47.191
provides us with
strength and guidance.


00:28:49.059 --> 00:28:53.546
Now, please, may we bow our
heads in silent prayer.


00:28:56.634 --> 00:28:57.966
Let us pray.


00:31:10.776 --> 00:31:11.943
Who are you?


00:31:11.944 --> 00:31:12.994
I'm-- It's--


00:31:12.995 --> 00:31:15.263
Are you a cop?
No.


00:31:15.264 --> 00:31:17.097
I was there when Allison died.


00:31:19.252 --> 00:31:23.621
This is where we used to come
and hang out all the time...


00:31:23.622 --> 00:31:25.822
listen to tracks
I was working on.


00:31:25.823 --> 00:31:27.756
I'm a DJ, so...


00:31:29.760 --> 00:31:33.597
You know, Allison said something
right before she died,


00:31:33.598 --> 00:31:35.382
and I'm just trying to figure
out what it means.


00:31:35.383 --> 00:31:36.683
What did she say?


00:31:36.684 --> 00:31:40.771
"He loved me."


00:31:40.772 --> 00:31:43.205
She said it like...


00:31:43.206 --> 00:31:44.974
she couldn't believe
this was happening to her.


00:31:44.975 --> 00:31:49.595
Like somebody she loved
really betrayed her.


00:31:49.596 --> 00:31:52.732
I don't know who Alli
was in love with,


00:31:52.733 --> 00:31:55.134
but it sure as hell wasn't me.


00:31:57.488 --> 00:31:59.322
How long had it been since you
talked to Alli?


00:31:59.323 --> 00:32:01.874
Months ago.


00:32:01.875 --> 00:32:03.092
Really? That long?


00:32:03.093 --> 00:32:05.893
Yeah, Alli and I, we dated,


00:32:05.894 --> 00:32:08.630
but that was like, 6 months ago.


00:32:08.631 --> 00:32:12.200
And we didn't talk since then.


00:32:12.201 --> 00:32:14.636
Alli was a mess,


00:32:14.637 --> 00:32:19.456
and she started going through
depression a year ago, and--


00:32:19.457 --> 00:32:21.058
She was depressed.


00:32:23.362 --> 00:32:25.346
Yeah, well, who isn't, right?


00:32:27.015 --> 00:32:30.117
I don't know. She started seeing
some quack doctor.


00:32:30.118 --> 00:32:32.253
I don't know what
they talked about, but--


00:32:32.254 --> 00:32:34.655
I don't know, we started
fighting all the time.


00:32:34.656 --> 00:32:36.490
You know, she started
blaming me for shit.


00:32:36.491 --> 00:32:40.693
For crazy shit. I just couldn't
take it anymore. I ended it.


00:32:40.694 --> 00:32:42.295
You ended it?


00:32:42.296 --> 00:32:44.214
Yeah.


00:32:46.116 --> 00:32:49.185
I mean, Alli, she was cool,
but she was out of her mind.


00:32:51.054 --> 00:32:54.290
I just bounced out of there
and I never looked back.


00:32:54.291 --> 00:32:57.927
Do you know if there was anyone
else in her life?


00:32:59.797 --> 00:33:01.597
No clue.


00:33:01.598 --> 00:33:04.033
That's between her...


00:33:04.034 --> 00:33:05.901
and God.


00:33:05.902 --> 00:33:06.902
And that shrink.


00:33:06.903 --> 00:33:08.720
Do you know his name?


00:33:08.721 --> 00:33:12.241
Doctor, uh...


00:33:12.242 --> 00:33:15.777
Bennett or... Barrett.
I don't know.


00:33:15.778 --> 00:33:18.046
She just always
called him "Graham."


00:33:22.701 --> 00:33:25.035
Thanks.


00:33:25.036 --> 00:33:26.988
Why do you care
who killed Alli anyway?


00:33:29.157 --> 00:33:30.424
Somebody has to.


00:34:06.760 --> 00:34:08.793
He loved me.


00:35:01.260 --> 00:35:02.445
Go on.


00:35:04.230 --> 00:35:06.165
Oh, um...


00:35:09.969 --> 00:35:12.505
Sorry-- I lost
my train of thought.


00:35:15.174 --> 00:35:16.407
It happens.


00:35:16.408 --> 00:35:19.910
I don't remember
what I was saying.


00:35:19.911 --> 00:35:21.378
It's okay.


00:35:21.379 --> 00:35:24.349
Sometimes we lose track
of what we're talking about.


00:35:24.350 --> 00:35:27.352
Our memories--
we get caught up in them.


00:35:27.353 --> 00:35:30.003
It was really vivid.


00:35:30.005 --> 00:35:31.705
You were talking about your
mother's illness?


00:35:31.706 --> 00:35:32.790
I was?


00:35:32.791 --> 00:35:34.724
Mm-hmm.


00:35:34.725 --> 00:35:35.826
My mother?


00:35:35.827 --> 00:35:37.411
Yeah.


00:35:37.412 --> 00:35:39.929
No, I don't think so.


00:35:39.930 --> 00:35:42.832
You wanna hide from this.
I know. It's okay. It's painful.


00:35:42.833 --> 00:35:46.252
But trust me, it'll hurt less
to keep talking.


00:35:46.253 --> 00:35:48.589
Yeah, I don't think so.


00:35:48.590 --> 00:35:51.675
Did you give up your apartment
when she became ill?


00:35:51.676 --> 00:35:56.378
Mm-hmm.


00:35:56.379 --> 00:35:59.382
Why? Because it was easier?


00:35:59.383 --> 00:36:01.884
To live with her while she was
undergoing her treatments.


00:36:01.885 --> 00:36:04.053
Look, I don't need
a pity party here, okay?


00:36:04.054 --> 00:36:06.939
I made choices.


00:36:06.940 --> 00:36:09.808
But like you said yourself,
you're all she had.


00:36:09.809 --> 00:36:11.743
No.


00:36:14.480 --> 00:36:15.881
What do you mean?


00:36:15.882 --> 00:36:18.083
You gave up your own life
to take care of her.


00:36:18.084 --> 00:36:19.716
How does that make you feel?


00:36:19.717 --> 00:36:22.386
That's not why I'm here.
I love my mother.


00:36:22.387 --> 00:36:23.654
This isn't about her.


00:36:30.512 --> 00:36:31.912
Happy birthday.


00:36:31.913 --> 00:36:33.381
What is this?


00:36:33.382 --> 00:36:35.966
Another day,
another body.


00:36:35.967 --> 00:36:37.484
No, no, no, no.
Give this to Gehrke. Come on.


00:36:37.485 --> 00:36:39.819
I can't. Reed put this on us.


00:36:39.820 --> 00:36:42.055
Didn't even say "pretty please."


00:36:42.056 --> 00:36:44.808
What?


00:36:44.809 --> 00:36:46.393
Something's not right here.


00:36:46.394 --> 00:36:49.078
How about we take a case
we can actually solve?


00:36:49.079 --> 00:36:53.750
There's something this nurse
said that just stuck with me.


00:36:53.751 --> 00:36:56.552
Maybe it was her
pretty blue eyes.


00:36:56.553 --> 00:36:58.955
Oh, and this looks like just a
random mugging.


00:36:58.956 --> 00:37:00.773
Maybe too much.


00:37:00.774 --> 00:37:03.224
It's like the attacker did
everything humanly possible


00:37:03.225 --> 00:37:07.279
to make this look like a
case-closed mugging gone wrong.


00:37:07.280 --> 00:37:11.266
I don't know.
Maybe she was onto something.


00:37:11.267 --> 00:37:13.301
The nurse that sees dead people?


00:37:13.302 --> 00:37:14.803
Yeah, we should definitely
substitute


00:37:14.804 --> 00:37:17.588
her judgement for ours.


00:37:17.589 --> 00:37:19.907
Maybe it was somebody
that she knew.


00:37:19.908 --> 00:37:22.344
Maybe it was somebody she knew
that disguised himself


00:37:22.345 --> 00:37:24.395
and made a conscious decision to
do it in a public place.


00:37:24.396 --> 00:37:25.696
Maybe he wanted to do it


00:37:25.697 --> 00:37:27.331
right in the centre of the
goddamn courtyard


00:37:27.332 --> 00:37:28.798
so there would be a witness,


00:37:28.799 --> 00:37:30.634
a witness that would testify
that it wasn't him.


00:37:30.635 --> 00:37:33.371
I'm gonna tell you the same
thing that you told me,


00:37:33.371 --> 00:37:35.272
the first day on the job.


00:37:35.273 --> 00:37:37.757
It's never that complicated.


00:37:39.476 --> 00:37:41.378
Why are you here?


00:37:41.379 --> 00:37:43.613
Well, I'd like to
talk about Allison.


00:37:45.283 --> 00:37:47.917
Ms. Parks' death
was an awful, awful thing.


00:37:51.105 --> 00:37:52.738
And, um...


00:37:52.739 --> 00:37:56.241
when something like that
happens, we feel...


00:37:56.242 --> 00:37:59.094
out of control, angry, helpless.


00:37:59.095 --> 00:38:00.729
These are normal things.


00:38:00.730 --> 00:38:02.898
It's perfectly normal
to feel these things.


00:38:02.899 --> 00:38:05.200
There's nothing you could do.


00:38:05.201 --> 00:38:06.601
There's nothing any of us
could've done.


00:38:09.089 --> 00:38:11.057
Who loved her?


00:38:11.058 --> 00:38:12.274
Hm?


00:38:12.275 --> 00:38:14.476
I think whoever did this
loved her.


00:38:14.477 --> 00:38:16.261
Do you have any idea
who it could be?


00:38:18.663 --> 00:38:20.365
I'm not about to talk to you
about my former patients.


00:38:21.917 --> 00:38:25.019
Besides, Allison
hasn't seen me in months.


00:38:25.020 --> 00:38:27.305
Why not? What happened?


00:38:27.306 --> 00:38:30.407
Was it depression?
Was there a boyfriend? Was it...


00:38:36.646 --> 00:38:38.182
I see our time is up.


00:38:38.183 --> 00:38:39.467
All right, wait a minute--


00:38:39.468 --> 00:38:41.300
But I do think it would be good
for you to come back


00:38:41.301 --> 00:38:43.320
and for us to keep talking.


00:39:00.354 --> 00:39:02.287
Mom? I'm home!


00:39:07.360 --> 00:39:09.295
Mom?


00:39:11.964 --> 00:39:13.899
Mom!


00:39:20.172 --> 00:39:22.106
Mom!


00:39:26.578 --> 00:39:28.513
Mom!


00:39:33.234 --> 00:39:35.169
Mom!
Katie?


00:39:36.938 --> 00:39:40.307
Mom!


00:39:40.308 --> 00:39:42.592
What? What is it, honey?


00:39:42.593 --> 00:39:45.195
I was just here and I--


00:39:45.196 --> 00:39:46.396
What?


00:39:46.397 --> 00:39:47.180
You were gone.


00:39:47.181 --> 00:39:48.698
What?


00:39:48.699 --> 00:39:52.218
I just-- I just walked in here,
and I didn't see you,


00:39:52.219 --> 00:39:54.821
and I thought--


00:39:54.822 --> 00:39:56.422
I thought maybe you had wandered
off or something.


00:39:56.423 --> 00:40:00.326
Wandered off? I wish.


00:40:00.327 --> 00:40:02.845
Honey, you should relax.


00:40:16.376 --> 00:40:20.312
Did you hang that
picture back up?


00:40:20.313 --> 00:40:22.614
You did.


00:40:22.615 --> 00:40:24.882
I did?


00:40:24.883 --> 00:40:27.085
Don't you remember?


00:40:29.671 --> 00:40:31.572
You told me to call you if I had
any new information.


00:40:31.573 --> 00:40:33.390
That's right.


00:40:33.391 --> 00:40:34.658
Should I come down there?


00:40:34.659 --> 00:40:37.311
No. No, here's no good.


00:40:37.312 --> 00:40:38.912
Why?


00:40:38.913 --> 00:40:41.715
Can we do this someplace else?


00:40:41.716 --> 00:40:43.216
Uh, you know the diner
by the hospital?


00:40:43.218 --> 00:40:44.750
I'm on my way.


00:40:44.751 --> 00:40:46.336
Great.


00:40:46.337 --> 00:40:48.622
What do you got?


00:40:48.623 --> 00:40:50.556
I've got a lead, pal.


00:40:53.227 --> 00:40:55.796
Wouldn't happen to be a blonde,
about 5'8", would it?


00:40:55.797 --> 00:40:57.913
It was unique.


00:40:57.914 --> 00:41:01.001
Kind of like this.


00:41:01.002 --> 00:41:02.402
Whoever killed her, took it.


00:41:02.403 --> 00:41:05.521
So, how do you know this?


00:41:05.522 --> 00:41:06.955
Did you see a broken necklace at
the crime scene?


00:41:06.956 --> 00:41:08.491
No, I didn't.


00:41:08.492 --> 00:41:10.324
Well, she wasn't wearing it when
she came into the ER,


00:41:10.325 --> 00:41:11.810
so find the necklace,
find the killer.


00:41:11.811 --> 00:41:14.529
Okay, well, it's not
that simple.


00:41:14.530 --> 00:41:17.548
Well, it's a clue,
so do something.


00:41:17.549 --> 00:41:19.585
Okay, I bust you snooping around
the crime scene.


00:41:19.586 --> 00:41:21.152
Suddenly you have inside
information.


00:41:21.153 --> 00:41:22.870
You have new evidence.


00:41:22.871 --> 00:41:24.606
Let's consider for the moment
that I'm not a complete idiot.


00:41:24.607 --> 00:41:25.972
You want me to believe you?


00:41:25.973 --> 00:41:27.342
Why don't you start
by not lying to me?


00:41:27.343 --> 00:41:28.676
I'm not lying to you.


00:41:28.677 --> 00:41:32.213
You're not telling me something.


00:41:32.214 --> 00:41:34.165
Try me.


00:41:39.588 --> 00:41:40.987
I'm having memories.


00:41:40.988 --> 00:41:42.822
What does that mean,
"memories?"


00:41:42.823 --> 00:41:45.125
I'm remembering the murder.


00:41:45.126 --> 00:41:47.610
I know things
I can't possibly know.


00:41:47.611 --> 00:41:49.512
It's like I'm reliving it
through her eyes,


00:41:49.513 --> 00:41:51.029
over and over again.


00:41:51.030 --> 00:41:53.582
I died that night too.


00:41:55.302 --> 00:41:59.087
Listen, in the ER, we hit
Allison with the paddles,


00:41:59.088 --> 00:42:01.656
and the electricity went through
her body and into mine,


00:42:01.657 --> 00:42:03.609
and my heart stopped.


00:42:03.610 --> 00:42:04.810
And once they revived me,


00:42:04.812 --> 00:42:06.145
I started seeing things
that weren't there,


00:42:06.146 --> 00:42:07.411
and having memories
that weren't mine.


00:42:07.412 --> 00:42:08.831
If you interfere
with this case again,


00:42:08.832 --> 00:42:10.166
I'm gonna be forced
to arrest you


00:42:10.167 --> 00:42:11.533
for obstruction of justice.
Do you understand that?


00:42:11.534 --> 00:42:12.850
Look, I know how crazy I sound.


00:42:12.851 --> 00:42:14.119
Do you?


00:42:14.120 --> 00:42:16.688
I do. Yes! I do.
But I'm not lying about this.


00:42:16.689 --> 00:42:17.989
And she was wearing
a necklace.


00:42:17.990 --> 00:42:20.126
No, I saw her wearing
that necklace.


00:42:20.127 --> 00:42:23.494
I saw the killer take it, and
run with it, and now it's gone.


00:42:23.495 --> 00:42:25.029
Okay, the perp
also stole her wallet.


00:42:25.030 --> 00:42:27.132
It would make sense
that he took any jewellery.


00:42:27.133 --> 00:42:28.549
It still fits the scenario
of a mugging.


00:42:28.550 --> 00:42:30.568
It wasn't a mugging.
This was personal.


00:42:30.569 --> 00:42:32.369
I saw him go for the necklace
like it was his,


00:42:32.370 --> 00:42:34.838
like he wanted it back
while he was stabbing me.


00:42:34.839 --> 00:42:37.941
Stabbing... her, you mean.


00:42:37.942 --> 00:42:39.259
Oh, yeah. Yes, of course.


00:42:39.260 --> 00:42:41.528
Of course.


00:42:41.529 --> 00:42:42.795
I think I can prove it.


00:42:58.460 --> 00:43:01.531
I knew it!
I knew your were a cop!


00:43:01.532 --> 00:43:03.166
Just have a couple of questions
for you, all right?


00:43:03.167 --> 00:43:04.917
So, what, you're gonna
arrest me now?


00:43:04.918 --> 00:43:07.820
Let's just keep the focus
on me for right now.


00:43:07.821 --> 00:43:11.090
Look, I already told you cops
everything. So what do you want?


00:43:11.091 --> 00:43:12.908
We want to know
about the necklace.


00:43:12.909 --> 00:43:16.528
I don't know anything
about a necklace.


00:43:16.529 --> 00:43:18.495
You've never seen this before?


00:43:18.496 --> 00:43:20.799
Yeah... That necklace.


00:43:20.800 --> 00:43:24.168
Yeah, I know that necklace.


00:43:24.169 --> 00:43:25.702
What?


00:43:25.703 --> 00:43:26.737
You give it to her?


00:43:26.738 --> 00:43:27.856
No.


00:43:27.857 --> 00:43:29.240
You know who did?


00:43:29.241 --> 00:43:32.627
Look, that was Alli's fave, man.
She wore it every day.


00:43:32.628 --> 00:43:34.628
I don't know. I thought
maybe she bought it.


00:43:34.629 --> 00:43:36.197
All I know is she never took it
off, once she got it.


00:43:39.600 --> 00:43:41.185
You mind if I go
through your gear.


00:43:41.186 --> 00:43:43.987
I don't have anything to hide.
You're not gonna find anything.


00:43:43.988 --> 00:43:45.555
You're not gonna find--
It's not like I have it.


00:43:51.545 --> 00:43:53.580
So, what? You're not a cop,
or what?


00:43:53.581 --> 00:43:56.349
No. I'm not.


00:43:56.350 --> 00:43:58.534
Well, so why do you know
about the necklace?


00:44:02.190 --> 00:44:04.540
What are you,
a psychic or something?


00:44:09.947 --> 00:44:11.596
Well, we need to
find this necklace.


00:44:11.597 --> 00:44:13.499
I thought you said
it wasn't that simple.


00:44:13.500 --> 00:44:16.450
Honestly, at the time, I didn't
think the necklace existed.


00:44:16.451 --> 00:44:18.437
So, what do we do now?


00:44:18.438 --> 00:44:20.238
Well, tell me about
these flashes,


00:44:20.239 --> 00:44:21.473
these visions, the clues.


00:44:21.474 --> 00:44:24.208
How do you have them?
What sets them off?


00:44:24.210 --> 00:44:25.860
I don't know, really.


00:44:25.861 --> 00:44:28.062
I thought I was going crazy.


00:44:28.063 --> 00:44:30.698
And sometimes I don't even know
that they've happened


00:44:30.699 --> 00:44:32.600
until after they're over.


00:44:32.601 --> 00:44:36.553
Well, we're about to
trigger one right now.


00:44:36.554 --> 00:44:40.524
If anything's going to set one
off, it's being here.


00:44:40.525 --> 00:44:43.226
This is exactly where
we found the body.


00:44:43.227 --> 00:44:47.147
So you, uh, you seeing anything?
Feeling anything?


00:44:47.148 --> 00:44:48.681
I don't think
it works like that.


00:44:48.682 --> 00:44:52.250
Okay, just relax, Kate.


00:44:52.251 --> 00:44:54.153
Try and remember. You've been
here before in your memory.


00:44:54.154 --> 00:44:58.140
So, right here, this is where
you ended up, right?


00:44:58.141 --> 00:45:01.744
Yeah, but I don't-- I don't
really want to see it again.


00:45:01.745 --> 00:45:04.663
We need this, Kate.
There's nobody else here.


00:45:04.664 --> 00:45:06.298
You're safe, okay?
Nothing bad is going to happen.


00:45:06.299 --> 00:45:07.532
Shit.


00:45:07.533 --> 00:45:10.586
Just walk me through it from
your perspective.


00:45:10.588 --> 00:45:12.720
She, what? She ran out?
She tripped? She fell?


00:45:12.721 --> 00:45:14.589
Yeah.


00:45:14.590 --> 00:45:16.558
Okay, and the guy is crouched
over, he's attacking?


00:45:16.559 --> 00:45:18.959
Yes.
Stabbing.


00:45:18.960 --> 00:45:20.244
Yeah.


00:45:20.245 --> 00:45:22.546
Okay. That's good.
That's good.


00:45:22.548 --> 00:45:26.550
Can you see his face?


00:45:26.551 --> 00:45:28.119
No, it's too dark.


00:45:28.120 --> 00:45:30.188
Okay, just-- just--


00:45:30.189 --> 00:45:32.090
close your eyes
and try and see it, Kate.


00:45:32.091 --> 00:45:34.592
You want me to close my eyes?


00:45:34.593 --> 00:45:36.160
Can you tell me
what he's wearing?


00:45:38.280 --> 00:45:40.113
Um...


00:45:40.114 --> 00:45:41.715
He's in black,


00:45:41.716 --> 00:45:43.716
and he's got a knife.


00:45:43.717 --> 00:45:45.386
Okay, good. That's good.
Can you describe it?


00:45:45.387 --> 00:45:47.422
It's a big knife.
It's a kitchen knife.


00:45:47.423 --> 00:45:50.557
And... the necklace?
You have the necklace on?


00:45:50.558 --> 00:45:55.496
Yeah. Yeah, it's around my neck,
and, um...


00:45:58.732 --> 00:46:02.301
And he yanks it, and takes off,
and then I wake up,


00:46:02.302 --> 00:46:04.069
and it's the same place,
every time.


00:46:04.070 --> 00:46:06.072
It's the same place
I wake up, every time.


00:46:09.826 --> 00:46:10.827
Okay. It's okay.


00:46:10.828 --> 00:46:12.928
It's okay. It's all right.


00:46:12.929 --> 00:46:15.263
He's been watching us
the whole time.


00:46:15.264 --> 00:46:18.317
Who?


00:46:18.318 --> 00:46:20.550
Please tell me you saw that.


00:46:20.551 --> 00:46:21.819
Okay, come on. Come on.


00:46:25.708 --> 00:46:27.442
We're never going to
find it here.


00:46:27.443 --> 00:46:29.645
Well, I'm gonna look anyway.


00:46:29.646 --> 00:46:31.145
He pulled it off
her neck, Peter.


00:46:31.146 --> 00:46:33.113
I got 14 eyewitnesses, Kaitlyn.


00:46:33.114 --> 00:46:35.215
The only one that saw something
is the one that wasn't there.


00:46:35.216 --> 00:46:39.754
So, humour me, please.


00:46:39.755 --> 00:46:41.322
I'm gonna check in the bedroom.


00:46:42.557 --> 00:46:44.091
Don't touch anything.


00:46:44.092 --> 00:46:48.929
Hey, Val. I'm sorry, I just got
wrapped up in something.


00:46:48.930 --> 00:46:50.646
Can you-- No, I'm fine.


00:46:50.647 --> 00:46:54.017
Yeah, my mom's fine too. There's
just something I need to--


00:46:54.018 --> 00:46:56.234
I gotta go.


00:47:02.342 --> 00:47:06.012
Any luck?


00:47:06.012 --> 00:47:08.214
No.


00:47:08.215 --> 00:47:13.051
You might be right.
I don't think it's here.


00:47:13.052 --> 00:47:14.319
So how do we find it?


00:47:14.320 --> 00:47:16.471
Well, I can add it to the
evidence report.


00:47:16.472 --> 00:47:18.206
With any luck, it'll turn up at
a pawn shop,


00:47:18.207 --> 00:47:19.775
and it's not particularly
valuable.


00:47:19.776 --> 00:47:21.643
There's a pawn shop
over by my apartment.


00:47:21.644 --> 00:47:24.012
I-- I-- I've got this covered.


00:47:24.013 --> 00:47:26.381
It's not your responsibility,
Kaitlyn.


00:47:26.382 --> 00:47:28.516
Do not let this
take over your life.


00:47:28.517 --> 00:47:29.818
I'm fine.


00:47:29.819 --> 00:47:33.254
I know. I know.
But I'm on this,


00:47:33.255 --> 00:47:35.207
with a new lead, thanks to you.


00:47:38.510 --> 00:47:40.278
So, what am I
supposed to do now?


00:47:40.279 --> 00:47:42.912
You're supposed to
take care of yourself.


00:47:44.799 --> 00:47:47.633
That's it. Come on.


00:47:47.634 --> 00:47:48.935
Come on.


00:47:51.172 --> 00:47:54.507
If I could, I'd like to bring us
back to your mother's illness.


00:47:56.960 --> 00:47:58.160
Big surprise.


00:47:58.161 --> 00:48:00.280
If you could, I'd like you


00:48:00.281 --> 00:48:02.381
to start talking about
how it felt


00:48:02.382 --> 00:48:04.016
when you first started
taking care of your mother.


00:48:04.017 --> 00:48:06.335
You know, the police
don't think Allison's murder


00:48:06.336 --> 00:48:08.403
was random anymore.
They found some new evidence.


00:48:08.404 --> 00:48:11.708
I just thought you might
find that interesting.


00:48:11.709 --> 00:48:13.993
Do you find it interesting?


00:48:13.994 --> 00:48:15.194
Yes, I do.


00:48:15.195 --> 00:48:17.196
And your mother's illness--


00:48:17.197 --> 00:48:19.097
Isn't.


00:48:19.098 --> 00:48:21.416
But I did what
I had to do, you know?


00:48:21.417 --> 00:48:24.052
She just got so sick so fast.


00:48:24.053 --> 00:48:27.922
There wasn't really time to
think about anything else.


00:48:27.923 --> 00:48:29.907
You know, like in the ER.
You don't think, you just react.


00:48:29.908 --> 00:48:32.478
She needed daily care,
and I wanted it done right,


00:48:32.479 --> 00:48:34.545
so... I don't know;


00:48:34.546 --> 00:48:36.814
moving in with her seemed
like the only solution.


00:48:36.815 --> 00:48:39.583
To be honest with you,
I didn't think. I just reacted.


00:48:43.555 --> 00:48:46.156
I wanna be there for her,
at the end.


00:48:49.193 --> 00:48:52.078
So, uh, yeah...


00:48:52.079 --> 00:48:54.247
I mean, yeah, it's--


00:48:54.248 --> 00:48:56.782
it's frustrating,
but she needs me, so...


00:48:56.783 --> 00:48:59.885
Do you feel like she's
a burden at all?


00:48:59.886 --> 00:49:04.156
No. Never.


00:49:04.157 --> 00:49:07.526
No resentment or anger
in your difficult situation?


00:49:07.527 --> 00:49:11.481
You're only human. I mean, it
doesn't mean you don't love her.


00:49:11.482 --> 00:49:16.335
She gave me everything.
She never asked me for anything.


00:49:16.336 --> 00:49:20.104
And you want me to sit here
and whine about it?


00:49:20.105 --> 00:49:22.141
God...


00:49:22.141 --> 00:49:24.175
I can see why Allison
stopped seeing you.


00:49:24.176 --> 00:49:25.409
Just trying to help you.


00:49:25.410 --> 00:49:27.695
When I moved in with my mother,


00:49:27.696 --> 00:49:29.496
she said she would never
be a burden to me,


00:49:29.497 --> 00:49:30.565
and she never was.


00:49:30.566 --> 00:49:32.500
That's good.


00:49:35.803 --> 00:49:37.471
I'm sure she just
wants you to be happy.


00:49:37.472 --> 00:49:39.422
Sometimes, accepting
your feelings--


00:49:39.423 --> 00:49:40.422
I found a gun, though.


00:49:40.423 --> 00:49:42.075
Gun?


00:49:42.076 --> 00:49:44.344
Yeah, I don't know
what kind it was.


00:49:44.345 --> 00:49:45.745
It was a handgun.


00:49:45.746 --> 00:49:47.914
I was looking
through her closets,


00:49:47.915 --> 00:49:50.583
going through some stuff,
and I found it in a shoebox.


00:49:50.584 --> 00:49:54.253
Didn't really make any sense,
because my mother hates guns.


00:49:54.254 --> 00:49:56.021
Eventually I found the receipt.


00:49:56.022 --> 00:49:57.790
She bought it the day
she was diagnosed.


00:49:57.791 --> 00:50:00.525
And what did you do?


00:50:02.529 --> 00:50:05.198
I got rid of it.


00:50:05.199 --> 00:50:07.866
Did you confront her about it?


00:50:13.273 --> 00:50:15.774
Kaitlyn, I think your
frustration with your mother


00:50:15.775 --> 00:50:17.209
and your inability to
communicate your feelings


00:50:17.210 --> 00:50:18.693
is what's fuelling


00:50:18.694 --> 00:50:20.361
your unhealthy obsession
with Allison.


00:50:20.362 --> 00:50:22.147
Fucking great.
Where do I send the cheque?


00:50:22.148 --> 00:50:24.432
You feel powerless
to help your mother,


00:50:24.433 --> 00:50:26.467
so you're struggling
to find a situation


00:50:26.468 --> 00:50:27.970
that you can take control of.


00:50:27.971 --> 00:50:29.771
She didn't deserve to die!


00:50:29.772 --> 00:50:33.441
She was innocent,
and nobody is fighting for her!


00:50:33.442 --> 00:50:35.209
They're just-- they're brushing
this thing off


00:50:35.210 --> 00:50:36.577
like it's something random,


00:50:36.578 --> 00:50:39.446
and I am the only one doing a
goddamn thing about it!


00:50:41.451 --> 00:50:42.934
Okay. Okay.


00:50:49.407 --> 00:50:51.908
I'm so tired. I can't think.


00:50:51.909 --> 00:50:54.510
Yeah, it's okay.
Just take a deep breath.


00:50:54.511 --> 00:50:58.030
Nice deep breath.
Breathe.


00:50:58.031 --> 00:50:59.682
You can say anything in here.


00:50:59.683 --> 00:51:01.751
You can think, feel,
anything in here.


00:51:01.752 --> 00:51:05.588
You're safe. It's okay.


00:51:05.589 --> 00:51:07.206
All right?


00:51:07.207 --> 00:51:09.207
We shouldn't do this.


00:51:09.208 --> 00:51:11.144
Oh...


00:51:22.756 --> 00:51:23.921
We shouldn't do this.


00:51:23.922 --> 00:51:26.958
It's okay, Allison.
It's only me.


00:51:42.691 --> 00:51:45.358
What about your wife?


00:51:45.359 --> 00:51:47.295
She can never find out.


00:51:57.404 --> 00:51:59.906
Help me.


00:51:59.907 --> 00:52:01.474
Get off me!


00:52:01.475 --> 00:52:03.293
You okay?


00:52:07.363 --> 00:52:09.398
We were lovers.


00:52:11.118 --> 00:52:13.285
Excuse me?


00:52:13.286 --> 00:52:15.119
Kaitlyn, are you okay?


00:52:15.120 --> 00:52:17.255
Don't touch me!
Don't you ever touch me!


00:52:23.963 --> 00:52:27.500
Man, please tell me you didn't
do what I think you did.


00:52:27.501 --> 00:52:29.585
Peter, I know who did it.


00:52:33.488 --> 00:52:35.422
Come here. Come here.
Come here. Come here.


00:52:35.423 --> 00:52:38.241
I told you we shouldn't
do this here.


00:52:38.242 --> 00:52:41.378
I found a murderer. Where do you
want me to go? A fire station?


00:52:41.379 --> 00:52:43.465
Okay, so you saw something.


00:52:43.466 --> 00:52:46.250
Yeah, Dr. Graham Barrett.
Allison's therapist.


00:52:46.251 --> 00:52:50.288
He's the killer. I've been going
there, pretending I'm a patient.


00:52:50.289 --> 00:52:53.290
Dammit, Kate,
do you hear yourself?


00:52:53.291 --> 00:52:54.858
Hey, don't throw this
in my face.


00:52:54.859 --> 00:52:57.060
I put myself in her surroundings
like your told me to,


00:52:57.061 --> 00:53:00.597
and it triggered something.


00:53:00.598 --> 00:53:02.698
This is not a game.


00:53:02.699 --> 00:53:04.468
I told you to lay off,
that I would handle this.


00:53:04.469 --> 00:53:06.635
Allison and Dr. Barrett were
having an affair.


00:53:06.636 --> 00:53:08.504
I saw it. I saw it as clear
as I'm seeing you.


00:53:08.505 --> 00:53:11.140
He kissed me-- I mean her.
He kissed her.


00:53:11.141 --> 00:53:12.040
He kissed you?


00:53:12.041 --> 00:53:13.725
Yeah, in the memory.


00:53:13.726 --> 00:53:15.361
I don't really know
how else to explain it,


00:53:15.362 --> 00:53:17.596
but he didn't want
his wife to find out,


00:53:17.597 --> 00:53:19.766
and I guess they started
this thing on the side,


00:53:19.767 --> 00:53:21.167
and then it got too serious.


00:53:21.168 --> 00:53:22.668
And then she threatened
to go to the wife--


00:53:22.669 --> 00:53:25.087
Yeah, and then he kills her to
keep her quiet.


00:53:25.088 --> 00:53:26.654
You have to arrest him,
right now.


00:53:26.655 --> 00:53:29.224
I can't arrest someone, Kate,
without evidence. I just--


00:53:29.225 --> 00:53:31.242
He killed her!


00:53:31.243 --> 00:53:32.743
Keep your voice down.


00:53:32.743 --> 00:53:34.778
Right now, all we have is your
word and your vision,


00:53:34.779 --> 00:53:37.815
which is all we have right now.
That's it.


00:53:37.816 --> 00:53:39.550
I thought you said
you believed me.


00:53:39.551 --> 00:53:42.502
I do believe you, Kate. I do.


00:53:42.503 --> 00:53:45.039
But there's protocol.
There's procedure.


00:53:45.040 --> 00:53:47.508
And unfortunately, your way
won't hold up in court,


00:53:47.509 --> 00:53:48.909
and it'll most likely
cost me my job.


00:53:48.910 --> 00:53:51.345
Please tell me
you understand that.


00:53:51.346 --> 00:53:53.113
I understand.


00:53:53.114 --> 00:53:54.464
You gotta let me
run with this, Kate.


00:53:54.465 --> 00:53:58.200
I'm not sure what I told him.


00:53:58.201 --> 00:54:01.922
In session, I blacked out for a
few seconds, maybe minutes,


00:54:01.923 --> 00:54:03.539
and I don't know what I said.
I don't know what he knows.


00:54:03.540 --> 00:54:05.341
What if he knows that
I know he's the killer.


00:54:05.342 --> 00:54:07.877
I mean, if he was willing to do
that to Allison,


00:54:07.878 --> 00:54:09.912
what could happen to me?


00:54:09.912 --> 00:54:12.531
Nothing.


00:54:12.532 --> 00:54:14.265
Nothing's gonna
happen to you, Kate.


00:54:14.266 --> 00:54:17.552
I won't let anything happen
to you, I promise. Okay?


00:54:29.697 --> 00:54:32.300
Is he still out there?


00:54:32.301 --> 00:54:34.301
Yeah, it's his job.


00:54:34.302 --> 00:54:36.271
Makes me nervous.


00:54:36.272 --> 00:54:38.439
Peter said he wanted to have
somebody watching us all night.


00:54:38.440 --> 00:54:40.374
He wants us to be safe.


00:54:40.375 --> 00:54:43.961
You better take him some coffee.


00:54:43.962 --> 00:54:46.079
Think so?


00:54:46.080 --> 00:54:49.533
Well, he's gonna be sitting
outside in the cold all night.


00:54:49.534 --> 00:54:52.786
We want him wide awake.


00:54:52.787 --> 00:54:53.987
It's the least we could do.


00:54:53.988 --> 00:54:55.922
All right.


00:54:59.527 --> 00:55:01.961
I know all about
your psychic nurse.


00:55:01.962 --> 00:55:04.397
Canto was right.
You are too close to this.


00:55:04.398 --> 00:55:07.083
Hey, Rafferty, this--


00:55:07.084 --> 00:55:09.502
We're not wasting any more of
the taxpayer's money.


00:55:09.503 --> 00:55:12.154
There's no reason to keep a car
outside the nurse's place


00:55:12.155 --> 00:55:13.640
all damn night.


00:55:28.004 --> 00:55:30.071
Man, I did it for your own good.


00:55:53.311 --> 00:55:55.245
Somebody order a coffee?


00:55:57.816 --> 00:55:58.982
What are you doing here?
What are you doing here?


00:55:58.983 --> 00:56:02.686
You are gonna give Allison a
message from me.


00:56:02.687 --> 00:56:04.288
Please get in the car.


00:56:04.289 --> 00:56:05.889
Please-- please don't get out
of the car. Please--


00:56:05.890 --> 00:56:06.905
I just want to talk.


00:56:06.906 --> 00:56:08.674
Are you drunk?


00:56:08.675 --> 00:56:13.128
I've been thinking
a lot about Allison, and...


00:56:13.129 --> 00:56:16.798
Do you, still talk--
do you talk to her?


00:56:16.798 --> 00:56:18.384
No, of course not.


00:56:18.385 --> 00:56:21.819
Yeah, but you're like one of
those psychics or something.


00:56:21.820 --> 00:56:24.823
No, could you please
get back in the car?


00:56:24.824 --> 00:56:26.391
Yeah, but I just
want to talk to her.


00:56:26.392 --> 00:56:28.275
Let go of me.
Let go of me!


00:56:31.330 --> 00:56:33.014
Aahh!


00:56:33.015 --> 00:56:35.749
You have the right to remain
silent. I suggest you use it.


00:56:37.069 --> 00:56:39.403
I just want to talk to Alli!


00:56:39.404 --> 00:56:40.772
You all right?


00:56:50.181 --> 00:56:51.181
You gotta cut him loose, man.


00:56:51.182 --> 00:56:53.515
I just need a little more time.


00:56:53.516 --> 00:56:56.636
You can't charge him. You can't
hold him. You know how it works.


00:56:56.637 --> 00:56:58.637
We didn't find shit in his
apartment, his car either.


00:56:58.638 --> 00:57:00.574
What about his alibi?


00:57:00.575 --> 00:57:02.192
Checked out.


00:57:02.193 --> 00:57:04.660
He was DJ-ing the night
that Parks was murdered.


00:57:04.661 --> 00:57:05.896
Yeah?


00:57:05.897 --> 00:57:07.581
30 witnesses can
place him at the scene.


00:57:07.582 --> 00:57:08.831
Might be a douchebag,


00:57:08.832 --> 00:57:10.599
but he's not our killer.


00:57:17.708 --> 00:57:19.641
So...


00:57:21.679 --> 00:57:23.244
You are a pathetic little
piece of shit.


00:57:23.245 --> 00:57:25.880
You're gonna stay away from her.
You hear me?


00:57:25.881 --> 00:57:27.983
I catch you within
half a mile of her


00:57:27.984 --> 00:57:29.834
and I swear to God I will break
every bone in your body.


00:57:29.835 --> 00:57:32.037
You hear me?


00:57:34.072 --> 00:57:35.523
Cut him loose.


00:59:00.671 --> 00:59:02.439
Hey.
Hi.


00:59:02.440 --> 00:59:03.573
You been okay?


00:59:03.574 --> 00:59:06.325
Yeah, you know... You?


00:59:06.326 --> 00:59:09.212
Been following the shrink.


00:59:09.213 --> 00:59:12.147
Care you see what I found?


00:59:12.148 --> 00:59:14.917
My mom's asleep. This might
not be the best time.


00:59:17.186 --> 00:59:18.820
Any suggestion on what
I should do with all of this?


00:59:22.274 --> 00:59:23.843
So this is Barrett's place?


00:59:23.844 --> 00:59:27.112
Yep. Lives with his wife
on the top floor.


00:59:27.113 --> 00:59:29.214
The night that Allison Parks
was killed,


00:59:29.215 --> 00:59:30.882
he had the whole place
to himself. No alibi.


00:59:30.883 --> 00:59:33.701
Really?


00:59:33.702 --> 00:59:36.872
Yeah, wife was out of town.
Some convention.


00:59:36.873 --> 00:59:39.206
Turns out she goes out of town
about once a month.


00:59:39.207 --> 00:59:42.377
Well, then, that must've been
when he had Allison over.


00:59:42.378 --> 00:59:45.579
That would be my theory
at the moment.


00:59:45.580 --> 00:59:47.197
We need to search his place.


00:59:47.198 --> 00:59:50.600
We need to find the necklace,
the knife... something.


00:59:50.601 --> 00:59:52.570
We do, but that requires a
search warrant.


00:59:52.571 --> 00:59:55.855
But you can get that.


00:59:55.856 --> 00:59:57.657
The press is already
watching me like a hawk.


00:59:57.658 --> 00:59:59.810
They think I'm working on
another case as it is.


01:00:02.480 --> 01:00:05.465
But...


01:00:05.466 --> 01:00:09.067
I can get one.
If that's what we need...


01:00:09.068 --> 01:00:11.538
I'll get one.
I don't know how,


01:00:11.539 --> 01:00:12.872
but I'll make it happen.


01:00:12.873 --> 01:00:15.174
Oh, and to think,
when you first met me,


01:00:15.175 --> 01:00:17.810
you were ready to toss me
in the loony bin


01:00:17.812 --> 01:00:20.212
and throw away the key.


01:00:20.213 --> 01:00:21.412
I was a little skeptical.


01:00:21.413 --> 01:00:23.282
Oh, a little bit? Okay.


01:00:23.283 --> 01:00:25.616
Well, thank you,


01:00:25.617 --> 01:00:27.570
for believing in me.


01:00:29.770 --> 01:00:31.372
No, thank you.


01:00:31.373 --> 01:00:34.109
For what?


01:00:37.512 --> 01:00:40.615
It's been a long time
since...


01:00:40.616 --> 01:00:42.649
since I believed in anything.


01:00:48.990 --> 01:00:50.758
Sorry...


01:00:52.326 --> 01:00:54.261
Sorry! I--


01:01:09.744 --> 01:01:11.844
I haven't snuck a boy up here
since high school.


01:01:18.052 --> 01:01:20.986
My mom is in the other room.


01:01:20.987 --> 01:01:23.188
Then we will
have to be very quiet.


01:03:46.858 --> 01:03:48.793
I haven't slept that well
in months.


01:04:00.305 --> 01:04:02.239
What's wrong?


01:04:05.343 --> 01:04:06.675
She's not there.


01:04:06.676 --> 01:04:10.212
What do you mean?


01:04:10.213 --> 01:04:14.483
Your mother.


01:04:14.484 --> 01:04:16.785
There's no one living
in that room.


01:04:19.089 --> 01:04:22.123
There hasn't been for a long
time, as far as I can tell.


01:04:22.124 --> 01:04:23.826
What are you talking about?


01:04:26.228 --> 01:04:28.163
Mom?


01:04:33.702 --> 01:04:37.672
Hey, Ma!


01:04:37.673 --> 01:04:38.973
What's wrong, honey?


01:04:38.974 --> 01:04:40.942
Nothing. Nothing.


01:04:40.943 --> 01:04:43.378
That's not fun--
You're not funny!


01:04:52.603 --> 01:04:54.604
Do you have someone over?


01:04:54.605 --> 01:04:57.907
It's Peter.


01:04:57.908 --> 01:05:01.277
Mom, uh, this is
Detective Peter Rafferty.


01:05:01.278 --> 01:05:03.546
Peter, this is my mom.


01:05:05.482 --> 01:05:08.351
Okay, now let's have some eggs.


01:05:19.228 --> 01:05:22.298
Patricia Monahan, aged 62,
died two months ago


01:05:22.299 --> 01:05:25.084
from complications
from pancreatic cancer.


01:05:25.085 --> 01:05:26.820
That doesn't make any sense.


01:05:26.821 --> 01:05:29.655
Yeah, well, I'm looking right
at her death certificate, man.


01:05:29.656 --> 01:05:31.022
Trust me, she ain't breathing.


01:05:36.663 --> 01:05:39.897
Thanks for covering for me,
the past few days.


01:05:39.898 --> 01:05:41.765
You feeling okay? You seem--


01:05:41.766 --> 01:05:43.501
What? Happy?


01:05:43.502 --> 01:05:45.603
I was gonna say "distracted."


01:05:45.604 --> 01:05:47.606
Oh, well, okay...
Peter, you know, the cop?


01:05:47.607 --> 01:05:50.374
He came over last night,
and he brought some food,


01:05:50.375 --> 01:05:52.243
and we had some wine--


01:05:52.244 --> 01:05:55.078
Sweetie, I am so sorry.


01:05:55.080 --> 01:05:57.981
Why? I thought you'd
be happy for me.


01:05:57.982 --> 01:05:59.916
Hello, Kaitlyn.


01:06:04.104 --> 01:06:06.473
Wait. Wait, wait...
what is this?


01:06:06.474 --> 01:06:09.691
It's good to see you again.
It's been a long time.


01:06:09.692 --> 01:06:11.176
No! Get away from me!


01:06:11.177 --> 01:06:12.511
She's just here
to help you get better.


01:06:12.512 --> 01:06:14.214
No, I don't need help!


01:06:14.215 --> 01:06:16.248
I don't need this!
Let go of me!


01:06:16.249 --> 01:06:18.634
You! What did you do?


01:06:18.635 --> 01:06:20.953
What did you tell them?


01:06:20.954 --> 01:06:22.622
What is going on?
What's going on?


01:06:22.623 --> 01:06:23.989
What did you do?


01:06:23.990 --> 01:06:26.174
I told them the truth.


01:06:28.060 --> 01:06:30.294
Get a hold of yourself,
for God's sake.


01:06:30.295 --> 01:06:32.731
I did everything. I did
everything you told me to do.


01:06:32.732 --> 01:06:34.933
Calm down, now. Calm down.
We talked about this.


01:06:34.934 --> 01:06:36.600
You can't just show up here.


01:06:36.601 --> 01:06:38.435
You said you would
stay with me.


01:06:38.436 --> 01:06:40.138
We were going to be
together forever!


01:06:40.139 --> 01:06:43.240
Allison, you stop it.
You shouldn't be here right now.


01:06:43.241 --> 01:06:46.410
You said you loved me.


01:06:46.411 --> 01:06:47.794
Allison, I said stop it!


01:06:47.795 --> 01:06:49.764
What is happening to me?


01:06:51.533 --> 01:06:52.666
Hey!


01:06:56.905 --> 01:06:58.773
What have they got me on?


01:06:58.774 --> 01:07:00.274
It's okay, honey.
Dr. Rosen's--


01:07:00.275 --> 01:07:01.875
No, I saw Dr. Rosen
and Dr. Barrett.


01:07:01.876 --> 01:07:04.711
He's-- he's trying
to keep my quiet.


01:07:04.713 --> 01:07:06.745
We're trying
to help you now.


01:07:06.746 --> 01:07:08.180
Okay? It's okay.


01:07:08.181 --> 01:07:09.715
Valerie, he's gonna
try and kill me.


01:07:09.716 --> 01:07:11.517
It's okay, honey.
Just relax.


01:07:11.518 --> 01:07:13.152
No, I--


01:07:13.153 --> 01:07:14.805
No!
It's okay.


01:07:16.323 --> 01:07:18.241
It's okay.


01:07:20.644 --> 01:07:22.810
It's okay.


01:07:26.233 --> 01:07:27.767
There you go, sweetie.


01:07:31.588 --> 01:07:33.738
There you go, sweetie.


01:07:48.135 --> 01:07:50.705
Go away.


01:07:50.706 --> 01:07:54.641
I'm sorry, Kaitlyn.


01:07:54.642 --> 01:07:56.810
You were the only one who
believed me.


01:08:01.148 --> 01:08:03.348
They're just gonna monitor you
for a few days.


01:08:03.349 --> 01:08:05.718
Just to make sure
everything is okay.


01:08:05.719 --> 01:08:07.354
Did you tell Dr. Rosen
you fucked me,


01:08:07.355 --> 01:08:09.455
or did you leave
that part out?


01:08:10.958 --> 01:08:12.892
What about my mother?


01:08:14.595 --> 01:08:17.129
What if she needs her shots,
and I'm not there to help her?


01:08:19.449 --> 01:08:21.184
You don't need to worry about
that right now.


01:08:21.185 --> 01:08:23.002
What does that mean?


01:08:23.003 --> 01:08:26.638
All that's important
is that you get healthy.


01:08:26.639 --> 01:08:29.174
That's it: that you
get back on your feet.


01:08:29.175 --> 01:08:31.076
I am healthy. I'm healthy!


01:08:31.077 --> 01:08:34.028
I don't need this!


01:08:34.029 --> 01:08:37.066
I am so confused. This doesn't
make any sense to me.


01:08:37.067 --> 01:08:38.300
Come on, we have
to help Allison.


01:08:38.301 --> 01:08:40.200
We've gotta find that necklace,


01:08:40.201 --> 01:08:42.237
and you have to
arrest Dr. Barrett.


01:08:42.238 --> 01:08:44.104
I'm not crazy, Peter.
You know that. You know!


01:08:44.105 --> 01:08:46.041
Come on, I'm not crazy.


01:08:48.644 --> 01:08:51.312
I had a memory.


01:08:51.313 --> 01:08:53.881
A real one. It was like the one
with the necklace.


01:08:56.951 --> 01:09:00.720
I want to show you something.


01:09:00.722 --> 01:09:03.574
I found this in
your mother's house.


01:09:03.575 --> 01:09:05.241
So?


01:09:07.612 --> 01:09:09.446
I know you took this from
Allison's apartment,


01:09:09.447 --> 01:09:11.431
the day I found you in the
courtyard. I know that.


01:09:11.432 --> 01:09:13.166
Yeah, I had a vision.


01:09:13.167 --> 01:09:15.902
The other picture fell,
and that led me to--


01:09:17.905 --> 01:09:19.921
Look at what she's wearing.


01:09:19.922 --> 01:09:22.557
You saw this in the photo.
Not in some vision or memory.


01:09:22.558 --> 01:09:24.060
You saw it in the photo,


01:09:24.061 --> 01:09:26.561
and then you subconsciously
tied it to Allison's murder.


01:09:28.480 --> 01:09:33.284
No, I'm-- I never saw that
necklace. Not that way.


01:09:39.592 --> 01:09:42.993
I care about you, Kaitlyn.


01:09:42.994 --> 01:09:46.730
I'll do whatever it takes.
I'm here for you.


01:09:46.731 --> 01:09:48.699
But you have to want
to get help.


01:09:50.653 --> 01:09:55.072
Hello, Kaitlyn. You came to see
me a couple of times


01:09:55.073 --> 01:09:59.309
when your mother first got sick.
Do you remember?


01:10:02.363 --> 01:10:06.233
How about we take these off?
Hm? And talk a little bit.


01:10:19.580 --> 01:10:21.214
Are you starting
to feel a little better?


01:10:27.820 --> 01:10:29.755
Okay.


01:10:43.568 --> 01:10:47.323
Detective Rafferty?


01:10:47.324 --> 01:10:50.141
She's suffering from severe
disorientation.


01:10:50.142 --> 01:10:52.776
I think the day her mother died
was so traumatic


01:10:52.777 --> 01:10:55.613
she's blocked it out.


01:10:55.614 --> 01:10:58.932
Now her mind is working to try
and explain everything all away.


01:11:01.102 --> 01:11:04.870
Over time, and in
the right environment,


01:11:04.871 --> 01:11:07.140
she'll find a way
to sort out what's real.


01:11:10.427 --> 01:11:11.694
Here's my card.


01:11:11.695 --> 01:11:14.630
It has my direct number.
As more questions arise...


01:11:17.433 --> 01:11:19.135
Thank you.


01:11:28.395 --> 01:11:30.261
Kaitlyn...


01:11:55.602 --> 01:11:58.255
Kaitlyn?


01:11:58.256 --> 01:11:59.291
Kate!


01:12:01.643 --> 01:12:03.427
Cop says to the hooker,


01:12:03.428 --> 01:12:05.461
"It's not polite to talk
with your mouth full."


01:12:10.201 --> 01:12:12.135
Yeah, it's Rafferty.


01:12:15.171 --> 01:12:16.572
Then where the hell is she?


01:12:53.091 --> 01:12:55.026
Kaitlyn!


01:12:57.661 --> 01:12:59.796
Kaitlyn, open up! It's me!


01:13:01.333 --> 01:13:03.300
Kaitlyn!


01:13:35.665 --> 01:13:38.667
Hi, Mom?


01:13:38.668 --> 01:13:40.736
It's not important.


01:13:40.737 --> 01:13:42.970
Are you okay?


01:13:42.971 --> 01:13:46.208
I know. Can you just hold on
a little bit longer?


01:13:46.209 --> 01:13:48.109
There's something I have to do.


01:15:16.243 --> 01:15:18.611
How did you get in here?


01:15:18.612 --> 01:15:21.964
I know what you did.
I know you killed Allison Parks.


01:15:23.734 --> 01:15:26.067
I saw it. I found this.
I saw it.


01:15:26.068 --> 01:15:27.736
I saw everything!


01:15:27.737 --> 01:15:29.304
How about we talk this through
like reasonable people?


01:15:29.305 --> 01:15:31.606
Think we can do that?


01:15:35.178 --> 01:15:37.879
Kaitlyn, I didn't kill anyone.
I didn't kill Allison.


01:15:37.880 --> 01:15:40.149
I found her necklace.


01:15:40.150 --> 01:15:41.932
I don't know what
you think that means.


01:15:41.933 --> 01:15:43.151
Proof!


01:15:43.152 --> 01:15:44.603
Proof of what?


01:15:44.604 --> 01:15:46.770
That I gave her a necklace
as an innocent gift?


01:15:46.771 --> 01:15:48.523
It's a clarity symbol.
I thought it would help her.


01:15:48.524 --> 01:15:50.475
She gave it back to me.


01:15:50.476 --> 01:15:53.578
No! No, stop lying!
I saw everything.


01:15:58.984 --> 01:16:01.085
What have you seen?


01:16:01.086 --> 01:16:03.603
I saw the way you treated her.
I saw the way you looked at her,


01:16:03.604 --> 01:16:07.457
the way you threw her away when
you were done with her, and now,


01:16:07.458 --> 01:16:09.592
now you're trying to do
the same thing with me, again.


01:16:09.593 --> 01:16:11.343
But that's not gonna work.


01:16:11.344 --> 01:16:13.996
I saw you! I saw you
murder Allison Parks!


01:16:18.568 --> 01:16:20.036
Let me help you.


01:16:20.037 --> 01:16:22.405
I know you think you're doing
the right thing here.


01:16:22.406 --> 01:16:23.805
I realize that,


01:16:23.806 --> 01:16:27.093
but I want you to listen to the
sound of my voice, Kaitlyn.


01:16:27.094 --> 01:16:31.264
You're suffering from something
we call post-event information.


01:16:31.265 --> 01:16:34.700
It's a-- after a trauma,


01:16:34.701 --> 01:16:37.536
your memories are vulnerable


01:16:37.537 --> 01:16:40.054
to facts and suggestions,


01:16:40.055 --> 01:16:43.558
ideas that you learn
after the tragedy has occurred.


01:16:43.559 --> 01:16:45.425
I saw you at the hospital
with Dr. Rosen.


01:16:45.427 --> 01:16:46.728
You don't know me.


01:16:51.984 --> 01:16:53.467
I didn't kill anyone.


01:16:53.468 --> 01:16:56.220
The mind is a complicated organ.


01:16:56.221 --> 01:16:59.155
Our memories are like
a jigsaw puzzle.


01:16:59.156 --> 01:17:00.924
But your mind is tricking you.


01:17:00.925 --> 01:17:03.810
It's creating puzzle pieces that
don't even exist right now.


01:17:03.811 --> 01:17:04.879
Shut up!


01:17:04.880 --> 01:17:06.596
Let me help you.
You need help.


01:17:06.597 --> 01:17:08.349
I know what I saw.


01:17:08.350 --> 01:17:10.333
I don't know what
you want from me.


01:17:10.334 --> 01:17:12.002
I want the truth.


01:17:12.003 --> 01:17:14.771
I want the truth about Allison.


01:17:14.772 --> 01:17:16.889
I want to know what's real.


01:17:20.461 --> 01:17:21.528
Real.


01:17:24.031 --> 01:17:25.965
You want the truth.


01:17:30.703 --> 01:17:33.122
Truth is that we had an affair.


01:17:36.960 --> 01:17:39.178
And I don't know how you--


01:17:39.179 --> 01:17:40.711
This was our secret.


01:17:42.915 --> 01:17:45.499
I didn't kill her.


01:17:51.122 --> 01:17:53.524
My wife and I, we were
having problems, and...


01:17:57.146 --> 01:18:00.863
One day, after a really
emotional session,


01:18:00.864 --> 01:18:02.799
Allison and I, we kissed...


01:18:10.623 --> 01:18:12.892
I know that was wrong.
I know it now.


01:18:12.893 --> 01:18:16.462
I never meant for it
to become serious,


01:18:16.463 --> 01:18:18.164
but it did.


01:18:18.165 --> 01:18:20.449
Hell, we ended up seeing each
other after every session.


01:18:20.450 --> 01:18:22.502
Why didn't you come forward?


01:18:22.503 --> 01:18:24.137
Why didn't you come forward when
she was murdered


01:18:24.138 --> 01:18:25.472
and tell people what you knew?


01:18:25.473 --> 01:18:30.493
Why would I want to put my wife
through all that, after?


01:18:30.494 --> 01:18:32.928
What would be the point?


01:18:36.599 --> 01:18:39.702
If the affair ever got out,
my career would be ruined.


01:18:39.703 --> 01:18:42.070
I would be finished.
Allison appreciated that.


01:18:42.071 --> 01:18:43.605
She said she understood that.


01:18:46.242 --> 01:18:48.375
When I went to break it off...


01:18:54.399 --> 01:18:56.734
She asked me to leave my wife,
and I told her I couldn't.


01:18:56.735 --> 01:18:59.069
She threw the necklace
back in my face,


01:18:59.070 --> 01:19:01.639
and she walked out the door,
and I never saw her again.


01:19:04.141 --> 01:19:08.745
That's the truth.


01:19:08.746 --> 01:19:11.781
You gotta believe me.
I would never kill Alli--


01:19:11.782 --> 01:19:13.783
I would never hurt her.
Not in a million years.


01:19:13.784 --> 01:19:17.686
I loved her.


01:19:17.687 --> 01:19:20.056
I love her still.


01:20:06.434 --> 01:20:10.053
Kaitlyn, wait, wait!
No, no, no, no...


01:20:10.054 --> 01:20:11.287
I got him.


01:20:11.288 --> 01:20:14.158
Okay, okay, okay. I need you to
put the gun down.


01:20:14.159 --> 01:20:15.190
Help me.


01:20:15.192 --> 01:20:17.961
I'm gonna put my gun down.


01:20:17.962 --> 01:20:19.062
He did it!


01:20:19.063 --> 01:20:20.462
I need you to put it down now.


01:20:20.463 --> 01:20:23.132
He killed her. You believe me,
right? That he killed her?


01:20:23.133 --> 01:20:24.133
I'm innocent!


01:20:24.134 --> 01:20:25.467
Shut up!


01:20:25.468 --> 01:20:27.970
Kaitlyn! Kaitlyn!


01:20:27.971 --> 01:20:29.905
Listen to me, you're confused
right now.


01:20:29.906 --> 01:20:31.623
Stop saying that to me.


01:20:31.624 --> 01:20:33.577
Kate, this is not
about Allison, okay?


01:20:33.578 --> 01:20:37.162
This is about your mother.


01:20:37.163 --> 01:20:41.550
Listen to me, you did everything
you could, Kate. You did.


01:20:41.551 --> 01:20:43.068
But sometimes,
it's just not enough.


01:20:43.069 --> 01:20:44.769
You know that.


01:20:44.770 --> 01:20:46.437
She loved me.


01:20:46.438 --> 01:20:51.425
This, Kate, this is not,
gonna bring her back, okay?


01:20:51.426 --> 01:20:55.897
Kate, I know what happened.
I read the medical files, Kate.


01:20:55.898 --> 01:20:58.115
I know what happened,
the day that she died.


01:21:03.054 --> 01:21:07.123
Did that stupid picture
fall again?


01:21:07.124 --> 01:21:08.441
I'll be right there.


01:21:08.442 --> 01:21:12.478
Your mother was sick, Kate.
She had cancer.


01:21:12.479 --> 01:21:15.849
There's not rhyme or reason
for it.


01:21:15.850 --> 01:21:17.951
Mom?


01:21:19.954 --> 01:21:22.155
Mom!


01:21:22.156 --> 01:21:25.424
Mom, hang on.


01:21:25.425 --> 01:21:28.594
Hang on! Hang on, Mom!


01:21:28.595 --> 01:21:30.161
Mom, stay with me, please!


01:21:30.162 --> 01:21:32.030
You're okay. You're okay.


01:21:32.031 --> 01:21:33.665
Mom, just a minute,
just a minute.


01:21:33.666 --> 01:21:38.404
Please, please, please hang on!
Hang on!


01:21:38.405 --> 01:21:41.357
Mom! Hang on, please!


01:21:41.358 --> 01:21:42.974
Mom! Please don't!


01:21:42.975 --> 01:21:44.976
Mom! Mom!


01:21:44.977 --> 01:21:47.278
No! Please don't!


01:21:47.279 --> 01:21:51.916
Mom! Please!


01:21:51.917 --> 01:21:56.037
No! No!


01:21:56.038 --> 01:21:58.239
Mom! Mom!


01:22:11.368 --> 01:22:14.888
I just-- I just-- I let her die.


01:22:14.889 --> 01:22:16.105
She loved me.


01:22:16.106 --> 01:22:17.973
She loved you.


01:22:17.974 --> 01:22:21.944
It's almost exactly what you
thought you heard Allison say.


01:22:21.945 --> 01:22:23.294
You see what's happening here?


01:22:27.869 --> 01:22:30.736
This man did not kill Allison.


01:22:30.737 --> 01:22:33.705
I know you'd like there to be
more to this, Kate,


01:22:33.706 --> 01:22:34.623
but there's just not.


01:22:34.624 --> 01:22:36.676
Your mother's gone, Kate.


01:22:42.465 --> 01:22:44.900
But there's absolutely
nothing...


01:22:44.901 --> 01:22:49.587
nothing that you
can do about this.


01:22:49.588 --> 01:22:51.821
Help me.


01:22:55.810 --> 01:22:57.729
I thought I told you nobody
could find out.


01:23:00.265 --> 01:23:02.583
Goddammit, Kate!


01:23:16.364 --> 01:23:19.316
Detective Rafferty. I need an
ambulance to my location.


01:23:19.317 --> 01:23:20.784
Shots fired. I have a man down.


01:23:20.785 --> 01:23:22.585
Please respond.
Priority three.


01:23:26.056 --> 01:23:28.591
Life is precious,


01:23:28.592 --> 01:23:31.811
but life is also
beyond our control.


01:23:34.965 --> 01:23:37.900
While difficult to accept,


01:23:37.901 --> 01:23:40.702
we often have little power
over such things.


01:23:47.425 --> 01:23:50.712
When our time comes,


01:23:50.713 --> 01:23:53.915
and our time must come,


01:23:53.916 --> 01:23:57.885
it does so without warning
or explanation.


01:24:14.586 --> 01:24:19.071
Thus we should embrace
every second


01:24:19.072 --> 01:24:23.442
we are allowed to remain
on this vibrant planet.

